    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a tool rather than a subject—useful for problem-solving in my part-time job, but I don’t find it deeply engaging like philosophy or computer science. My parents taught me basic skills, and though I understand concepts now, I struggle with abstract proofs due to its structured nature. It’s practical but not an obsession.",
